{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_109a5e847d816ce1754fcfc79c183c2be56f93f187917029de41383be3dc63c8"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Hybrid search is designed to fail open to lexical results with truthful metadata, and lexical publish uses atomic swap/retention semantics that must not be bypassed."},{"claim_ids":["clm_31043c1a5824fd53811fcc3fe206217ebee6d7bfde3ee343cfc4b9f4509e6cbf"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"frankensqlite-backed SQLite storage is the durable source of truth, while lexical and semantic search assets are treated as derived state rebuilt from it."},{"claim_ids":["clm_3facd194f76ab95f5f0e27cbca895b78fe47b2eed0b2d94f9785dffd80d7b803"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: AGENTS.md is authoritative for repo-local safety rules including no file deletion, no destructive git/filesystem commands, no new rusqlite, and no script-based code rewrites."},{"claim_ids":["clm_6b1904770a1c00dab97d68a30f68cede318cb5635112c72df6da8017d6b046a6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: refactor passes follow one lever per pass with one commit each, a proof card, and a fresh-eyes review prompt before closeout, while avoiding peer-dirty high-blast-radius files like indexer and storage."},{"claim_ids":["clm_8fa0eab95bdd69795ce40223e6b1ed98adb29171bef9dd0c99e68945c0db22ea"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"cass exposes a human/TUI surface plus a robot-mode JSON API, with stable robot JSON schemas, error kind values, and exit codes treated as user contracts."},{"claim_ids":["clm_bead293f6fc9391d43054144e36b96740b23bac43deb581f0af24319ca03b877"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"New SQLite code must use frankensqlite rather than adding new rusqlite, which is described as legacy debt in the storage layer."},{"claim_ids":["clm_cb25b36eb2fd33a049bc4e96f740b6c7f9e258ab12b6c2124c224a2cc04dce85"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Connector modules are compatibility re-export stubs over franken_agent